e/apply misfired (the 33). (3) Reconciliation (uncommitted): compile-guest-call routes entry-PRESENT callees through admission (admitted→bridged, forged→refused) and entry-ABSENT callees (collections, raw closures) to invoke-value — itself invoked as a proper common call (yang.call/invoke + escape-based raise mirroring bridged's capture/resume); `fn?` restored to the adoption definition; `::invoker` detection tightened to the invoke-value name; the gate round's try/->/fresh-supply/kind-seam work kept. (4) astra r1 (thread 01a199e5) DENIED with two P2 blockers: dispatcher re-entry (apply inside invoke-value recursed into the routing → 30k-instruction exhaustion on scalar/raw-closure callees) and the entry test checking truthiness not presence (`{:yang.call/entry nil}` would lookup). (5) v2: invoke-value refuses via `(throw (yang.call/condition :yang.call/not-callable {...}))` (no apply anywhere), routing test is map-guarded key presence (`(if (data/map? c) (data/contains? c :yang.call/entry) false)`), and new `test-value-invocation-refusals-are-terminating` (library-enabled, walker+semantic): scalar exact-shape refusal, module-fn admission (measured: the linker compiles module fns as ADMITTED descriptors — `(yang.call/entry f)` legitimately succeeds; the projected raw closure refuses), nil/false entry presence refusals, tail-position refusal, operands-before-check in both positions via a guest throw (native refusals escape as host exceptions outside adapter seams — probed and discarded). Focused lane 122/0; kondo 0/0 both files.\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:112:Done: (1) The astra design round returned the APPROVED hardening-3 plan (collab/1793770000000-architect-hardening-3-design.gpt-6-astra.*): seven slices — H3-0 restore declared dispositions + trustworthy evidence (lands first, harness-only); H3-1 diagnose the two blocked fixtures (finding: all three blocked C executions hit \"Guest instruction budget exhausted\" at 2,0