tra.stdout.log) returned: do NOT adopt position-only selection as written — it breaks the LANDED clj_apply callback leg (cross_lang_test.clj:100, a TS closure passed as a parameter has no projected-name position) and the §8.10.11 contract (\"pass, return, store, recurse, call back\"); the scissor framing was overstated (a wrong-seal imitation IS heap-distinguishable; only an exact copy of a valid ref is indistinguishable — and that is a working bearer reference by design); verdict: retain the two operations, rule for a generic non-fatal authentication effect reusing the engine's existing authentic-ref? (engine.cljc:331), with five rules (strict explicit resolution; runtime authentication in ordinary application; authentication ≠ authorization per the :2120 pin; bearer copies retain behavior; static specialization is optimization-not-semantics). (2) The owner asked what \"authentication effect\" means; seat grounded it in the codebase: the cell module is an effect language (pure constructors + engine interpreter, module.cljc:378); authentic? = a fourth constructor + one interpreter case returning (authentic-ref? state :cell/ref ...) non-fatally — the query voice of the predicate that today only speaks as check-ref!'s fatal gate. Owner: \"oh i see. monadic effect ... ok. i like this idea. lets go with your recommendation\" — RULING ACCEPTED. (3) Ruling-of-record written (collab/yang-clojure/1794330000000-architect-cell-ref-ruling-of-record.md): the seven rules incl. scope decisions (entry-key policy OUT — rule 7; the bag clarification: storage changes nothing, the authentication query at the call decides) + required §8.10 documentation + the acceptance battery. (4) r5 dispatched to glm-5.3 (the owner's lane for this unit): the two scoped VM hunks, routing consults authentic? (shape = cheap pre-filter for WHEN to ask, never decides meaning), astra's reconciliation checklist binding (call.cljc:23 _descriptor, clojure.cljc:1245/1403/1458, ts prelude:135 + lower:1167, py prelude:1033, php prelude:4229), the collision-literal + bearer-copy + exposure-probe regressions, the docs. (5) BLAST-RADIUS ANALYSIS for the owner (grounded by grep): VM additive only (no vocabulary pins exist; state/protocol unchanged; the boolean oracle leaks nothing the fatal check didn't); the shared _descriptor definition is the CONTAINMENT mechanism (fix once, all convention frontends inherit); shape-routing sweep = 4 files (PHP doesn't route cell-ref shape — doc only); behavior delta strictly widening (aborts become answers; genuine refs unchanged). TWO DOMINO CANDIDATES: (a) benign-by-design — clojure_test.clj:2131 pins the superseded refusal semantics and must be rewritten to the ruled answer-as-data behavior; (b) VERIFY — latte_oracle_test registers the cell module, so IF the kernel gate's candidate inventory counted VM-module functions, authentic?/1 would enter as unexercised (20→21) and H3-3 could never fully unblock the gate; the seat's reading is the inventory is latte-kernel-scoped (all 20 entries are latte-kernel.*), and the remote 4M gate rerun in r5 verification will confirm the counts unchanged (102/2/2 + the same 20). Both candidates go into the codex gate brief so the reviewer checks them independently.\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:550:Done: (1) The remote battery on the STRIPPED tree (jupiter, CURRENT-STRIPPED): matrix 13/21/0 (incl. the collision-literal regression), full yang.clojure-test 95/922/0, yang.base 126/0, the NEW yin.vm cell-test 17/197/0. The revert verified EXACT (empty diff vs f35c65c2 on both prelude files — the accepted kind-of fix intact). (2) DOMINO-B VERIFIED on jupiter: the 4M kernel gate on the stripped head {:pass 109, :recorded-upstream-failure 2, :recorded-deviation 2}, fixture-count 113, manifest-bindings 155, function-arity-candidates 175, unexercised function/arities = 20 — IDENTICAL to pre-r5; wall 349s; the single by-design :gate-status failure. The oracle inventory prov