mplemented, verified, and landed Slice H4 per dao.stream.host-boundary.md r10/r11 (§2.4, §3.1, §4.2 table B, §8 H4, §8.1, §8.2, §14):\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13477:Next: owner browser check at http://192.168.1.2:3004/ (shop; /grid editor, no auth). Reviewer confirmation of the two new features available on request.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13769:Done: three concurrent lanes launched beside the two S3 engineer rounds: (1) the P5 architect commission to fable (session c42e2f91, plan mode) - P5 depends only on P1 per the slice table, so its plan runs during P4 engineering; (2) the P4-seam compute on shiva (tmux p3b-seam): the FULL permutation oracle recording via corpus full + the php-src phpt selection - both were gate-declared P4-seam conditions and are pure shiva compute; (3) the cross-language substrate demonstration (sonnet, session in the xlang prompt; branch yang-cross-lang-demo off master): a TS closure called from PHP-lowered code and the reverse, with the opacity/null non-identity limits pinned as documented expectations - the empirical evidence slice for the section 8.10 story discussed with the owner this session. Operational note recorded: a trailing & inside a backgrounded dispatch DETACHES the child (it survives; the wrapper completes empty) - the failure mode differs from a kill; check process liveness and log growth before re-dispatching, and never re-dispatch under a live session id (the collision error is the tell).\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13855:Decisions: the number-kinds correction propagates to the future 8.10 ABI work: the portable-value tier is narrower than assumed (booleans/strings TBD; numbers need a conversion rule or bigint acceptance).\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:158:(§8.1), as a foreign engine's layout is, and does not enter A.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:223:where `L(p)` is the standard live-in set at the resume pc `p` (§8.1),\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:557:   liveness of §8.1 is computed over the real successor relation, in\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:724:`saved(pc, rd)` from A (§8.1) and refuses a window with a register\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:778:from A (§8.1), and keeps `:yin.safepoint/layout` as a map from physical\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:838:checksum are regenerated then, mechanically (derivations design §8.1-8.2).\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:863:### 8.1 Static facts per pc: def, use, live\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:928:     windows are `saved(p, rd)` at *reachable* safepoints (§8.1), and\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:949:     operands (step 3) and every saved window come from §8.1's\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:965:   virtual live-out over the instruction's **actual successors** (§8.1)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:1024:at the slice and once at cutover (derivations design §8.1); nothing is\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:1061:descriptors lose their lift declaration (derivations design §8.1-8.2);\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:1084:   loader rules of §3.4 (both load paths), **and the §8.1 analysis\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
