er's request: same error, request_id c6cdab06-ebc3-44da-bca0-b52065caf2ed. Both -contrib ids fail on this account; plain muse-spark-1.3 works and carries the implementation lane. If the contrib lane is intended, the account needs the access grant or the exact catalog id from the owner's console. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\n2026-11-04 0x:xx +0700 — the correct contrib id is muse-spark-1.3-contributor; it EXISTS but shares the exhausted quota (resets 2026-11-09)\\nOwner-directed probe: muse-spark-1.3-contributor resolves (no \\\"does not exist\\\" error — unlike muse-1.3-contrib and muse-spark-1.3-contrib, which are wrong ids) but returns \\\"quota exhausted. Your usage window resets at 2026-11-09\\\". The whole muse account lane (plain + contributor) is walled until Nov 9. Implementation substitution decision escalated to the owner: kimi-implements + sol-reviews (recommended; kimi landed P7-a/P5/P9/xlang green this session) vs parking implementation until Nov 9. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\n2026-11-04 0x:xx +0700 — owner relays: kimi is OUT of credits; muse-spark-1.3-contributor works now; gpt-6.1-sol is the architect\\nCurrent lanes for this track: IMPLEMENTATION = muse (muse-spark-1.3-contributor); ARCHITECT/REVIEW = codex gpt-6.1-sol (owner-confirmed twice). kimi unavailable (credits) — its architect/gate duty moves to sol. agy remains quota-walled (~Nov 9-10); codex implementation is not used while sol is the named architect (family-independent review preserved: muse implements, sol reviews). Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\n2026-11-04 12:4x +0700 — owner: muse cli is available on shiva — PROBE CONFIRMED (contributor model, rc OK despite bwrap warnings)\\nMeasured: muse exec on shiva with muse-spark-1.3-contributor returns OK. The Linux sandbox still cannot use bwrap (missing --ro-bind-symlink capability; install under writable /home/sto flagged) — muse runs UNSANDBOXED there with wa