{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^##|''^###|caller|site|UAST|schema|version'\"' collab/yang-clojure/1794630000000-engineer-attribution-as-query.prompt.md\"","aggregated_output":"5:# Task: implement the SIGNED attribution-as-query ruling — caller-side site tagging, derived site tables, the seven-case battery, the honest migration\n9:## Context\n11:Worktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-aaq, branch attribution-as-query, base master 3eebe844e (the ruling landed; D2, cell/authentic?, H3-2, H3-3 all in). The governing reviews (astra/qwen/kimi) are linked from the ruling's header — kimi's v3 review found the mechanism flaw your implementation must respect: **site ids are CALLER-SIDE, at application expressions in the compiled AST, post-macroexpansion; the callee-entry record carries the CALLER's site id.** Callee-side tagging (v3's flaw) yields identical records for both origins and is forbidden.\n13:## The implementation, in the ruling's stated order\n15:1. **FIRST DELIVERABLE — the written inventory confirmation**: what the instrumentation change touches (kernel-trace-form's position, the walker's application-node stamping site, the callee-record extension), the capacity measurement (stream/make + the instruction bound vs the added trace field — R6), and the offset-table coverage list (every context-API arity kernel-context-extra-arguments served, latte_oracle_test.clj:1786). Write it BEFORE code; commit it as the round's first commit.\n16:2. **Caller-side site-id stamping**: application expressions in the compiled AST (post-macroexpansion — the corpus runs under is/testing/LaTTe macros; source-level tagging misses expanded sites) get compile-time-unique site ids; the callee-entry record becomes `[fname arity caller-site-id]`. The walker changes are AUTHORIZED by the ruling (R2) — scoped to application-node stamping + the record extension; nothing else in yin.vm moves.\n17:3. **Mechanically derived site tables**: the compiler derives each site's argument shape (ambient literal `empty-env` vs anything else) during instrumentation — the tables are DERIVED, not hand-declared (R7's trust model), recorded in a stable versioned evidence format (R1's condition b), with the canonical-source-hash per fixture (R2b case 3's referent).\n23:## Verification (test-boundary ruling: focused local, suite-scale remote)\n29:## Boundaries\n31:- yin.vm: ONLY the application-node stamping + the callee-record extension (R2's authorization). No other VM changes. yang.clojure: untouched unless the stamping requires it (justify). The harness (latte_oracle_test.clj, context.edn, slice9_gate.md's versioned attribution section) is the main surface. The pin migrations are authorized by R5 — list every revised pin in the evidence.\n34:## Report\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
