budget,    |\n1554:| J2: pure test lane and VM conformance       | `test:jolt`       | Every applicable pure test loads and passes; semantic and register boundary traces match. No silent |\n1565:| J2b: deferred comparisons                   | Oracle/lowering   | Node/Dart oracle comparison and restricted lowering comparison (§7.8); both close before J5. Owner  |\n1566:| closed (zero pins, JVM canonical)           |                   | split from J2, 2026-10-22 (§13.5); JVM canonical, divergent hosts patched (owner 2026-10-24).       |\n1574:|                                             | catalog, shell    | selectable since J5 (the native C++ parser, §7.6 budget).                                           |\n1582:| J4 closed 2026-10-28;                       |                   | never overwritten; no J4-owned entry remains in jolt-applicability.edn or the J2 lane; cross-host   |\n1590:|                                             | ness-probe        | Amended (row 59): enforced input/nesting budget, stage-owned worker lifecycle and the               |\n1592:|                                             |                   | 16 MiB parse thread (§7.6). J5b budget/crash legs (bb probe:jolt-j5, bb calibrate:jolt-j5) on       |\n1594:|                                             |                   | the owner's \"linux only\" waiver. J5c (deterministic work budget) ledgered; precondition for         |\n1603:|                                             | contract, CBOR    |                                                                                                     |\n1608:|                                             | datagram contract |                                                                                                     |\n1637:J0a, J0b and J0c are independently commissionable and reportable; their\n1693:their portable behavioural equivalents and cross-process peer legs are required.\n1697:lane table remains open. `test:jolt-core` includes `^:slow`; J2 gate (b) remains\n1699:pending (`a0a49b8e`; `docs/agents/known-gaps.md`, J2 classification rows).\n1711:budget. At J8: startup cold/warm/devboot/AOT, submission latency, large-integer\n1782:|            |                                       | never silently. No numeric JVM-ratio budgets until J8 evidence.                                                  |\n1786:| Q7         | \"keep landed contract\"                | No UDP `full`. Would-block (EAGAIN/EWOULDBLOCK, macOS ENOBUFS) is transport-error plus the send-failed event; no |\n1868:  resolved jolt closure. J2: codec-less compositions fail at composition on\n1880:  `append!`; the contract forbids a waiting operation and the transport's\n1956:closure. Evidence: `a0a49b8e` (J2 lane and its owner-ruling comments),\n\nC preprocessing, Rust macro expansion, SQL dialect resolution, TypeScript\nchecking, and Ruby dynamic dispatch are plugin-owned stages. Each has\nexplicit inputs, outputs, and dependencies. None requires Yang core to\nrecognize its language by name.\n\n### 8.10 Shared function calling convention\n\n**Status: proposed, 2026-10-29; not implemented.** This section specifies\none invocation convention for every conforming ANTLR-based Yang frontend.\nExamples are non-exhaustive. Adding a language must not add a case to Yang\ncore, a language-pair bridge, or an evaluator transition. The words\n**must**, **must not**, and **may** state requirements on a future\nconforming implementation, not claims about current code.\n\n#### 8.10.1 Decision and scope\n\nA Yin function is a Yin function, independent of its source syntax. The\nVM applies a closure to operands. Source calling semantics are ordinary\nUAST implementing the call site and callee entry, above the VM.\n\nEvery supported source-level callable, after its source-required\nresolution, exposes `:yang.call/entry`, an ordinary Yin closure taking\nexactly one invocation record. Invoking it is an ordinary\n`:application`. No AST tag, lambda slot, instruction, host primitive,\neffect kind, or source-language test is added to the VM.\n\nThis is an internal calling convention, not a transport, another system\nABI, or a host callback interface. Calls between source languages inside\none task do not themselves cross a host boundary. Portable I/O and\ncross-task interaction continue through `dao.stream`.\n\n**Transparent calling** means that an admitted callable can be passed,\nstored, returned, and invoked by any conforming frontend without a\nhandwritten language-pair wrapper. It does not mean every foreign value\nsatisfies every source operation. Invocation, name visibility, and value\nrg: src/cljc/yin/vm/ast.cljc: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nsrc/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc:4:   `:application`, `:if`, `:vm/current-continuation`); nothing here adds a\nsrc/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc:17:     (yin/def k v)     -> the definition application\nsrc/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc:18:     (f a ...)         -> :application\nsrc/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc:41:  {:type :application, :operator op, :operands (vec args)})\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
